# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local, machine-specific configuration. This repo is intended to go public:
# nothing in config/ is committed except the *.example templates.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
config/*
!config/*.example
!config/README.md

# Secrets, in case anything lands outside config/
*.env
!*.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.token
tokens
secrets
secrets/
debug-notes/
auth.json

# Output of a rebuild test run. Evidence for the run that produced it and
# stale the moment the repo changes -- and a committed one is the next
# fresh-context agent's first read, which is the opposite of the point.
# Keep them in archive/ if you want them.
REBUILD-RESULT*.md
MACOS-RESULT*.md

# Agent + VM state that must never be committed
.pi/
.hermes/
.openclaw/
*.log

# Pi transcripts from scripts/pi-session.sh. Worth reading, not worth
# committing: they are long, machine-specific, and quote config paths.
logs/

# The handoff bootstrap.sh writes for the supervising coding agent. Local
# state about one build, regenerated on every run.
NEXT-STEP.md

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Artifacts pulled out of the VM (contain local detail)
dist/

# Anything local to this machine and deliberately not shared. local/souls/
# holds hand-written SOUL.md content migrated from another deployment -- a
# one-time exception to "the repo ships a seed, never a managed file" (see
# the Agent personality section of AGENTS.md). It is personal, it names
# people, and it must not be mistaken for something this repo installs.
local/

# Pre-simplification snapshot of the repo (2026-10-29). Local reference
# only -- git history is the real record. See archive/2026-10-29/README.md.
archive/
